{"author":{"id":"85a3c31a64931f83958f26b24045fef8415ea6ff04d942d15661891c77fc0695"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1794216935,"nonce":"bj0/FBsj0LOX+KPUyOYbwweZq8Y=","message":"Remaining items landed in the working tree (uncommitted):\n- Swizzle assignment, plain and compound (c.xz = v, c.wy += v): each component stored on its own from a value computed before the first store; a swizzle naming a component twice is an error.\n- Array lengths from constants: integer arithmetic, casts and parentheses over literals and constants, imported ones included, evaluated in the front end from the constants' source. A pipeline constant cannot size an array (it is set per pipeline). Array repeat expressions [x; N] too.\n- Uniform layout: WGSL's uniform address-space rules checked in the analyzer with the error at the field: 16-byte array strides, struct members on 16-byte boundaries, and the member after a struct leaving its size rounded up to 16. Storage buffers are unaffected. Types::size_align holds WGSL's size and alignment.\n- f16 literals lower to naga's Literal::F16 (via half, the crate naga uses), integer literals that become f16 included; a module using f16 has no GLSL ES 3.00 and says so in glsl_missing.\n- Compile-fail tests through rustc with trybuild (crates/russl/tests/ui): a type error, a Rust module with no russl module, a shader warning denied with #![deny(deprecated)], an unknown pipeline constant in a variant. Expected output is stable rustc's (stable underlines only the first token of a span; nightly joins them), so the test skips on nightly.\nTests: tests/language.rs (9) in the compiler, a macro test of the features through rustc.\n\nThis closes the issue's scope and its gate: golden WGSL tests that naga validates for every target, and compile-fail tests on the error spans.","files":null}]}